{
    "a_galaxy_workflow": "true",
    "annotation": "This workflow performs multi-sample binning of metagenomic assemblies with CONCOCT, MaxBin2, MetaBAT2, SemiBin and optionally COMEBin, using cross-sample read coverage, and refines the bins with DAS Tool and/or Binette",
    "comments": [
        {
            "id": 0,
            "type": "markdown",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
                100,
                165
            ],
            "size": [
                8370,
                260
            ],
            "data": {
                "text": "## Multi-sample binning\n\n**Coverage:** flatten the original read pairs, form an assembly × read-sample cross product, then rebuild paired collections and matching references with Apply Rules. These operations reuse the original FASTQ datasets. Bowtie2 maps every sample to every assembly.\n\n**Binning:** summarize all sample alignments per assembly into coverage matrices. Enabled SemiBin, CONCOCT, MetaBAT2, MaxBin2 and COMEBin branches use cross-sample coverage. CONCOCT read length is estimated automatically from both mates.\n\n**Refinement:** prepare contig assignments for DAS Tool and candidate FASTAs for Binette. Return selected refined bins, quality reports and coverage matrices. Disabled branches are handled through optional bridges."
            }
        },
        {
            "id": 1,
            "type": "frame",
            "color": "blue",
            "position": [
